{
  "name": "Ley Collector",
  "icon": "tribalpower:ley_collector",
  "order": 20,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:ley_collector",
      "text": [
        "A generator that drinks the planet's ley lines. Set it where a line passes, among open sky, water, plants and life, and it adds Pulse every **two seconds** without you standing there.",
        "It holds **2,000 Pulse**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What it listens to",
      "text": [
        "Every two seconds the collector adds one **beat** of Pulse. A beat starts at **1**, and the land within **8 blocks** (the same range as the lattice) adds more:",
        "- Open sky: **+1** by day, **+3** at night.",
        "- Rain **+2**, and a thunderstorm **+1** more.",
        "- Water: up to **+4**.",
        "- Plants: up to **+4**. Every four grass, leaf, flower, crop or moss blocks count as one.",
        "- Totem voices: up to **+3**, one per distinct voice.",
        "- A Tribe Hearth **+1**. Animals: up to **+2**, one per pair.",
        "- In the March **+2**; under a full moon **+1**.",
        "Those gifts are the land's share, and that share is capped at **6**. The rest of the beat is the ley line the collector is touching: **+2** for each line. The lines themselves are a web across the world; only the rarest places bring **six** together, and a collector never counts more than that. The beat is still capped at **16**. The number a Ley Lens shows is that beat, not Pulse a second. Hold the lens to see the lines themselves.",
        "A Resonance Totem pulls the thread of its own colour through itself, and leaves the other colours alone. Set the six totems around a collector so each thread crosses it on the way through its totem. That is a convergence: six colours, and still no more than six lines on the beat."
      ]
    },
